---
// About Narrative Composition (T-013 text/AI note; T-014 photos, refined
// after developer visual review against Figma, then real photos +
// ambient-logo repositioning) — about-narrative/technical-design.md. One
// single-template composition (Owned Concepts: "single-template
// completeness invariant") — narrative paragraphs, the AI-assisted-
// development note woven in as the final paragraph (Commitment 2 —
// subordinate positioning guaranteed structurally by authored order, never
// conditional placement logic), both personal photos (Commitment 4 —
// plain, non-interactive <img> elements; no carousel/toggle/enlargement
// affordance exists to trigger), and the Ornamental Logo's large-scale
// ambient background instance (Commitment 5 — non-interactive,
// subordinate, no completeness dependency of its own).
//
// Purely static, no client-side hydration: none of Commitments 1, 2, 4, 5
// need runtime state. Text is passed in already resolved by the
// i18n/Routing Layer for the active route's locale — this component never
// reads the Content Layer or decides the language itself (Commitment 3).
// Each paragraph is its own element (ux.md, Feature Components) so the
// separately owned `motion-interaction` Feature has individual pieces to
// target later; this component defines no motion of its own.
//
// Layout direction (developer visual review, post-implementation): the
// first pass boxed the two photos into a small, isolated side column —
// read as "pasted," not part of the content. Redesigned as a single
// centered column (both device classes — one render path, per
// technical-design.md's own Design Decision) with the photos rendered
// large, gently rotated and slightly offset, folded directly into the
// paragraph rhythm rather than parked in their own strip alongside it —
// still plain <img> elements with no card/border framing (ui.md,
// Component Anatomy), just position/rotation, which isn't framing.
//
// Real photos (developer-supplied, replacing placeholders): imported via
// `astro:assets` rather than referenced as raw `public/` files, so Astro's
// build-time image pipeline (sharp) resizes/compresses them instead of
// shipping the 5MB source JPEG as-is. `--landscape`'s actual supplied
// photo is itself portrait-oriented (746x1115) despite the class name —
// kept for continuity with ux.md's own "the portrait photo"/"the
// landscape photo" vocabulary (these name the two content pieces, not
// strictly their pixel orientation); its aspect-ratio below matches the
// real photo rather than forcing a lossy 4:3 crop. Worth flagging: ux.md's
// Content and Assets calls for "contrasting orientations" — both supplied
// photos are portrait, so that specific note isn't literally satisfied by
// this asset pair; not a defect in this component, a real-content
// observation for whoever selects final photos.
//
// Photo order (developer direction, post-implementation): the landscape-
// slot photo now renders first (near the opening line) and the
// portrait-slot photo second (near paragraph 4) — the reverse of ui.md's
// own "the portrait photo is anchored near the opening line, the landscape
// photo positioned lower" ordering. This is a deliberate, explicit
// developer override of that specific ui.md line, not a reinterpretation
// of it; ui.md itself isn't updated to match (out of this component's own
// artifact ownership), so this comment is the record of the divergence.
//
// The Ornamental Logo is the same shared asset `section-navigation`
// already references at its own compact scale (public/ornamental-logo.svg)
// — not redefined here, only placed. Repositioned (developer direction) to
// sit behind the three paragraphs between the two photos specifically —
// moved from a section-wide absolute position into `.narrative__middle`'s
// own stacking context, so it centers on that content group by structure
// rather than a hand-tuned percentage of the whole section's height.
//
// sectionIntro: new copy, authored directly with the developer in
// conversation (not previously in ux.md's Content and Assets) — a short,
// low-key section kicker, grounded in the Figma reference's own "get to
// know me." label (Figma node 13:2/20:13, evidence only, not previously
// transcribed into approved content). Flagged here for the developer to
// adjust freely; distinct from the six-paragraph Narrative Text component,
// so it doesn't reintroduce the heading/label component ui.md's Component
// Anatomy excludes from the narrative text itself.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portraitPhoto from './portrait.jpg';
import landscapePhoto from './landscape.jpg';

interface Props {
	heading: string;
	sectionIntro: string;
	paragraphs: string[];
	photoPortraitAlt: string;
	photoLandscapeAlt: string;
}

const { heading, sectionIntro, paragraphs, photoPortraitAlt, photoLandscapeAlt } = Astro.props;
const [paragraph1, paragraph2, paragraph3, paragraph4, paragraph5, paragraph6] = paragraphs;
---

<div class="narrative">
	<h2 class="narrative__heading">{heading}</h2>
	<div class="narrative__text">
		<p class="narrative__kicker">{sectionIntro}</p>
		<p class="narrative__paragraph narrative__paragraph--opening">{paragraph1}</p>
		<Image
			class="narrative__photo narrative__photo--landscape"
			src={landscapePhoto}
			alt={photoLandscapeAlt}
			width={500}
			loading="lazy"
		/>
		<div class="narrative__middle">
			<img class="narrative__ambient-logo" src="/ornamental-logo.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
			<p class="narrative__paragraph">{paragraph2}</p>
			<p class="narrative__paragraph">{paragraph3}</p>
			<p class="narrative__paragraph">{paragraph4}</p>
		</div>
		<Image
			class="narrative__photo narrative__photo--portrait"
			src={portraitPhoto}
			alt={photoPortraitAlt}
			width={700}
			loading="lazy"
		/>
		<p class="narrative__paragraph">{paragraph5}</p>
		<p class="narrative__paragraph">{paragraph6}</p>
	</div>
</div>

<style lang="scss">
	@use '../../styles/tokens' as tokens;
	@use '../../styles/mixins' as mixins;

	.narrative {
		position: relative;
		// Rotated photos (below) bleed slightly past their own box — contain
		// that bleed the same way Hero contains its own mark's bleed, rather
		// than letting it force horizontal scroll.
		overflow: clip;
		// Deliberately taller than the shared $space-lg other section edges
		// use — Hero fills the full viewport height, so this section's own
		// top padding is the *only* breathing room between them (developer
		// visual review: felt cramped straight off Hero's bottom edge).
		padding-top: tokens.$space-xl;
		padding-bottom: tokens.$space-lg;
		padding-inline: tokens.$space-md;
	}

	// Visually hidden but AT-reachable — the section's own landmark
	// heading (accessibility Commitment 4, AC2), distinct from the
	// visible kicker below (which is decorative section-intro copy, not
	// this landmark). Feature UI's Component Anatomy deliberately
	// excludes a visible heading/label component for the narrative text
	// itself; exact heading authoring is this Task's own
	// implementation-level decision (accessibility/technical-design.md,
	// Commitment 4 AC2/AC4), so this stays inaudible-to-sighted-visitors.
	.narrative__heading {
		position: absolute;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		margin: -1px;
		padding: 0;
		overflow: hidden;
		clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
		white-space: nowrap;
		border: 0;
	}

	// Single centered column on both device classes — one render path
	// (technical-design.md, Design Decisions), not a left-column/
	// right-thumbnail split: reads as one composed, centered moment
	// rather than a document with an illustration parked beside it
	// (developer visual review). Photos (below) sit in this same flow,
	// in DOM/reading order, so completeness (Commitment 1) and the
	// portrait-near-opening / landscape-near-a-later-paragraph
	// relationship (ui.md) both come from authored order alone, holding
	// regardless of how far each locale's translated paragraphs reflow.
	.narrative__text {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: tokens.$space-lg;
		max-width: 38rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		text-align: center;

		@include mixins.desktop-up {
			gap: tokens.$space-xl;
		}
	}

	.narrative__kicker {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: tokens.$font-family-body;
		font-weight: tokens.$font-weight-label;
		font-size: tokens.$font-size-caption;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: lowercase;
		color: tokens.$color-accent;
	}

	.narrative__paragraph {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: tokens.$font-family-body;
		font-weight: tokens.$font-weight-body;
		font-size: tokens.$font-size-body;
		line-height: tokens.$line-height-body;
		color: tokens.$color-base-fg;
	}

	// Opening line's elevated emphasis (Feature UX/UI: "the composition's
	// greeting moment") — weight/size only, no colour or family change
	// (ui.md, Colour Application: "the opening line's emphasis comes from
	// size/weight alone"). Sized as its own extension midway between the
	// shared body tier and the heading tier — text-length-appropriate for
	// a full sentence, not a literal transfer of Hero's two-word headline
	// size (ui.md, Typography Application); exact ratio is this Task's
	// own Implementation Detail, since Feature UI names no concrete value.
	.narrative__paragraph--opening {
		font-weight: tokens.$font-weight-display;
		font-size: calc((#{tokens.$font-size-body} + #{tokens.$font-size-heading}) / 2);
	}

	// Groups paragraphs 2-4 (the block "between the images") as the
	// Ornamental Logo's own positioning context (below) — its own gap
	// reproduces `.narrative__text`'s gap exactly, since wrapping these
	// three items into one flex child would otherwise collapse the parent
	// gap that used to sit between each of them individually.
	.narrative__middle {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: tokens.$space-lg;
		width: 100%;

		@include mixins.desktop-up {
			gap: tokens.$space-xl;
		}
	}

	// Ornamental Logo — large-scale ambient background instance
	// (Commitment 5; technical-design.md Responsibilities/Owned Concepts;
	// ui.md Spacing and Layout — "Rendered as a background layer, behind
	// all narrative content in stacking order"). Same shared asset
	// `section-navigation` already references at its own compact nav
	// scale; only placement/scale/opacity are this component's own
	// concern. Centered on `.narrative__middle` (developer direction:
	// behind the three paragraphs between the two photos specifically) —
	// `position: absolute` with no explicit z-index paints behind that
	// wrapper's own normal-flow paragraph children by default stacking
	// order, without needing z-index on either side. aria-hidden and
	// pointer-events:none since it carries no interactive/focusable
	// behavior of its own (Commitment 5, AC1) and no positional
	// relationship to any specific paragraph (ux.md) — ambient atmosphere
	// behind a content group, not aligned to any one paragraph within it.
	.narrative__ambient-logo {
		position: absolute;
		top: 50%;
		left: 50%;
		transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
		width: min(60vw, 34rem);
		height: auto;
		// Asset's own gradient already fades toward transparent; this
		// opacity is the "extremely low opacity ambient texture" ui.md
		// calls for on top of that, so it reads as atmosphere behind the
		// text rather than a second visible mark.
		opacity: 0.14;
		pointer-events: none;
	}

	// Plain, non-interactive image elements — no carousel/lightbox/toggle
	// affordance exists to change or enlarge them (Contract Commitment 4),
	// and no card/border framing (ui.md, Component Anatomy: "no
	// card/border framing"). Sized large and set at a gentle rotation with
	// a small horizontal nudge — a deliberately candid, snapshot-tucked-
	// into-the-page feel (developer direction: "experimental," "playful,"
	// "part of the content") — rather than a neutral boxed thumbnail. Both
	// are presented simultaneously since neither is conditionally
	// rendered.
	.narrative__photo {
		display: block;
		height: auto;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.narrative__photo--portrait {
		width: min(75vw, 20rem);
		aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
		transform: rotate(-4deg) translateX(-0.5rem);

		@include mixins.desktop-up {
			width: 22rem;
		}
	}

	// Aspect-ratio matches the real supplied photo (746x1115 ≈ 2/3), not a
	// generic 4:3 landscape box — see file-top note on why this slot's
	// actual photo is itself portrait-oriented. Sized narrower than
	// `--portrait` (its own real aspect ratio is taller per unit width) so
	// the two photos read as comparable visual weight rather than one
	// towering over the other.
	.narrative__photo--landscape {
		width: min(65vw, 16rem);
		aspect-ratio: 2 / 3;
		transform: rotate(3deg) translateX(0.75rem);

		@include mixins.desktop-up {
			width: 18rem;
		}
	}
</style>
